      "message": "Some background for anyone interested (and a question at the end).\n\nWIP and private evolved out of \"drafts\", where [Shawn was clear](https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/gerrit/+/62340/comment/84bfd6dd_57dc0c77/) that even if a user could view drafts, they shouldn\u0027t get the project watch notification. That was later broken in change I6a8e2f62f. This is the snippet of Shawn\u0027s justification:\n\u003e We do not want to notify anyone when a new draft is created. A draft is just that, its a draft. It shouldn\u0027t be reviewed like a normal change.\n\u003e \n\u003e If you have View Draft permission you can search for and find this draft, but we aren\u0027t going to automatically notify you until it gets published.\n\nThey\u0027re a little different from drafts, but it seems like that logic would still apply to both WIP and Private changes. @samccone@google.com is that your thinking too? If yes, maybe just make that clear in the commit message.",
